Claim type: bounded_theorem

A quantitative Lie-basis certificate turns the supplied finite one-port compiler into an explicit positive-duration recipe. For a fixed plant, fixed path strength and fixed certified commutator basis, its pulse count and duration have polynomial upper bounds in inverse approximation tolerance. Their constants and exponents can be enormous. The theorem provides neither a polynomial algorithm in qubit count nor a uniform result as the coupling or certificate conditioning deteriorates.

Primary-runner role: source integrity only. The proposed 60-second primary verifies exact sources, recovery intervals, canonical-parent identities and actual root binding evidence. It runs no pulse search, matrix fixture, numerical simulation or scientific proof checker. The historical source proposal remained unexecuted. This separately bound version requires actual root publication-review and selected-base receipts. Primary, cache, source mutation, graph, publication and retained-audit outcomes remain separate actual records; binding alone certifies none of them.

Qualified scientific source acceptance is `9f90d834ef33e01300eed265e196df1f8d66ec92f846bfa96d30716d7d25790d`. The complete root derivation `2de387eb…`, protected derivation `dd6cca85…` and subsequent exposed comparison `227180a0…` follow unchanged. Root's actual source acceptance ran at 21:00:28.385–21:00:28.490 UTC on 2026-10-15; its metadata receipt is preserved. This wrapper applies the accepted chronology, norm-test and timing qualifications without rewriting the proofs. Root separately accepted this publication interpretation at exact review 0cdc01cd5b26bc48f250e5a854d93cb41ed3c135ae1a7dfed24be9d0e7d8c8fd; actual integration remains a distinct recorded decision. The selected PR 9621 on physics-loop/toe-polynomial-path-mediator-20261015 is Git ancestry only and adds no theorem or supplier premise. The distinct accuracy-scaled-coupling proposal is explicitly excluded and has not been read or imported here.

## 1. Physical problem, actual target and sole parent

Let the nonempty fixed plant contain every original data, apparatus, memory and clock factor, together with every added dirty filler. Its dimension is `d>=2`. Let `H` be the literal complete supplied computable onsite/ordinary-nearest-neighbor background, including the original `H0` and any `K_X` retained for this invocation. Supply `h>=||H||` and the actual coefficients, not only the norm. `H` need not commute with the target or controls. Every plant factor and arbitrary correlated passive reference is retained.

The inherited geometry encloses the fixed original sites in a rectangular integer box with one empty margin layer, adds a qubit at each missing box site, and orders all `L_P` sites in an alternating-row/plane Hamiltonian path beginning at a fresh corner port. No original factor moves. The `L_P-|V_old|` fillers have arbitrary states and correlations. Install

```
J=sum_(path edges)(I-SWAP),       j=2(L_P-1),
0<=J<=jI,                       j0=Tr(J)/d=(L_P-1)/2,
Jbar=J-j0I,                     b=3(L_P-1)/2>=||Jbar||.
```

Each of the `L_P-1` path bonds is positive with norm two, and at most two are incident to a site. Additional coefficients on an already occupied old edge do not create an extra geometric neighbor. For side lengths `n_x,n_y,n_z`, the full box has `(n_x-1)n_y n_z+n_x(n_y-1)n_z+n_x n_y(n_z-1)` geometric edges. Nonzero declared edges are the union of old supports and path supports; every remaining box edge and exterior interaction is nominally zero or charged in the full-space defect. No infinite unmodeled environment is assumed isolated for free.

The sole mathematical parent is the [qualified finite one-port compiler](SINGLE_PORT_PROGRAM_AND_AUTONOMOUS_CONTROLLER_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-10-15.md), canonical SHA256 `9b08b7a78f21390d065322150d1fe6a222343323cc76dfe7f3b065a624d5a18e`, published as regular PR 9617 at head `86eac8cc4523f7f15c8d84824f462f9a5c037806`. Only its complete compiler proof `bda0be88…` and assessment `3ad0ab65…` are imported. The same note's autonomous-controller proof is not an import. Other campaign PRs provide no mathematical premise here, and the future Git stack base is deliberately unset.

Fix actual `lambda>0`, port strength `g>0`, and time unit. The physical nominal dynamics are

```
H_ph(t)=H+R_s I+lambda J+C(t),
C(t)=g f(t)(I+sign P_p),   P_p in {X_p,Y_p}, 0<=f<=1.
```

At most one port pulse is active; zero is allowed. Every pulse is positive, vanishes with zero derivative at segment boundaries, and is zero during a declared output window. The externally supplied waveform is `C1`. The static reserve `R_s>=h` makes the entire nominal generator positive. It does not make every literal old local term a separate positive channel.

Writing `H=h0 I+Hbar`, and `W=e^(i theta) Wtilde`, the chronological comparison at the compiler's actual elapsed duration `T` and subsequent time `s` is

```
U_tar(T+s)=exp[-i chi(T+s)] exp(-isH) W exp(-iTH),
chi(T+s)=(R_s+lambda j0)(T+s)+A_s+theta,
A_s=integral_0^T g f(t)dt,                 0<=s<=w.
```

Thus original-background aging precedes the ideal endpoint program and follows it during the window. In general the target is not `W exp[-i(T+s)H]`. The scalar `h0` is already in the literal `H` flows. The determinant lift `theta` belongs to the comparison phase, not to physically applied Hamiltonian action. The physical preparation is continuous; this endpoint comparison does not say that the program actually occurred instantaneously.

## 2. Quantitative certificate and two distinct target contracts

Define the five augmented skew-Hermitian generators

```
X_a=diag(-i t0[Hbar+lambda Jbar+v_a], -i t0 Hbar),
v_a in {0,+gX_p,-gX_p,+gY_p,-gY_p}.
```

The direct sum of dimension `2d` records plant evolution and the same actual background time. It is mathematical bookkeeping, with no physical second plant or initialized auxiliary. In the root recipe units have `t0=1`.

Supply `d^2-1` formal binary commutator trees, each of leaf degree at least two, evaluating exactly to `diag(B_l,0)` and forming a real basis of `su(d)` in the first block. The zero second block is exact because all primitive second blocks coincide. Supply a norm bound `M` and a quantitative conditioning certificate at the actual selected `lambda`. Projected controllability alone is insufficient for the printed constants. The inherited existence of suitable finite trees is not a cost bound for discovering or certifying them.

| Contract | Additional target data | Certificate normalization | What is bounded |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Root supplied-logarithm construction | Computable traceless skew `Q` with Frobenius norm at most `L_Q`, and `theta` with `W=e^(i theta)e^Q` | Rational smallest singular-value lower bound `sigma>0` in a Frobenius-orthonormal real basis; rational `b_l` bounding the operator norm of `B_l` | Coefficient rounding, signed-word count, finite recurrence count, rational positive duration and smoothing |
| Protected finite-grid construction | Computable full unitary `W` and computable determinant lift `theta`; no logarithm oracle | Rational `kappa>=1` bounding the coordinate one-norm by `kappa` times the operator norm of `Z=sum c_l B_l` | A finite target coefficient-grid search as well as the full positive-duration recipe |

A singular-value certificate implies `kappa>=sqrt[(d^2-1)d]/sigma`; the constants must be converted explicitly before reuse. The two constructions have different Taylor constants and resource recipes. Agreement of their conclusion does not identify their numerical bounds or give independently replicated compiler runs.

The finite grid uses existence of a traceless logarithm with norm at most `pi(d+1)` only to prove coverage. It enumerates bounded rational coefficients and accepts a strict certified Frobenius-distance margin. It does not select a computable spectral logarithm branch. Both finite searches require certified computable matrix/norm approximations; their finite candidate counts are separate from arbitrary input-oracle bit complexity.

The actual drift `Hbar+lambda Jbar` acts during every segment and long recurrence wait. No smallness assumption on `lambda T` is used. The recipe chooses its own completion time; it does not solve control at an arbitrary prescribed deadline. The known target may be `W_old tensor I_fillers`, with no initialization assumption on those fillers.

## 3. Load-bearing positive-time mechanism and resource recipes

For a bracket tree define `W_[U,V](u)=W_U(u)W_V(u)W_U(u)^(-1)W_V(u)^(-1)`. Its first nonzero Taylor term is the specified bracket times `u^r`, where `r` is total leaf count. The signed list is only an algebraic intermediate. The complete bodies prove explicit finite Taylor remainders, split the target into small basis exponentials, and telescope unitary errors. Matrix-order products are implemented by the reversed chronological list.

In the root contract set `eta=epsilon/16`, `B=sum b_l`, `C=1+L_Q/sigma`, `K=CB`, and take a dyadic coefficient mesh `eta/[2(1+B)]<delta<=eta/(1+B)`. If `r=max r_l`, `n_l` is the recursive primitive-word length, and `E_l` is the printed rational Taylor majorant, use exactly the sufficient choices

```
D=sum E_l C^2,
m=ceil(max(1,C,K^2/eta,(D/eta)^r)),
L<=m sum n_l,
q=ceil(16L/eta),
T<=4L q^(2d),
rho_min=min(delta/(8m), eta/(gL)).
```

The all-rounded-coefficients-zero case uses an empty schedule, `T=0`, and no smoothing; no theorem requiring positive runtime is invoked. For `L>=1`, each negative factor is replaced using a finite recurrence of the entire augmented matrix, with durations at least one in the selected time unit. Rational duration rounding changes both blocks to the new actual `T`; ramps are inserted within those same intervals. The endpoint coherent error is at most `11eta<epsilon`. The recipe gives pulse count `O(epsilon^-r)`, duration `O(epsilon^-[r+2d(r+1)])`, and inverse ramp width `O(epsilon^-(r+1))` at fixed admitted data. Optional rational ramp widths within a factor two double the stated slew allowance.

For the protected contract use its distinct tolerance `eta`, maximum tree degree `ell`, and explicit constants `C_N,C_Q` from its sections 2–7. Its finite coefficient grid has `O(eta^-(d^2-1))` candidates. Its displayed sufficient recipe gives

```
N<=C_N eta^-ell,
Q<=C_Q eta^-(ell+1),
T<=2t0 C_N C_Q^(2d) eta^-[ell+2d(ell+1)],
1/(t0 rho)<=[8C_r/t0+16gC_N] eta^-(ell+1).
```

Each of five recurrence searches has at most `Q^(2d)` candidates. Both blocks recur together. Root's smaller `q` supports its certified **operator-norm** recurrence test; substituting a Frobenius test at that same threshold may introduce a factor `sqrt(2d)`. The protected construction uses its explicitly larger `Q` for a Frobenius test. Those ceilings and acceptance norms remain distinct. Root pays for rational segment-duration rounding; the protected construction retains exact computable durations and its exact signed-balance expression for total time. Further rationalization would require an additional paid error and phase update. Its smoothed endpoint coherent error is at most `15eta/32`, and the complete unhalved plant/reference trace error is

```
min(2, 2[15eta/32+lambda b w+E_int]),
E_int=integral_0^(T+w) ||E(t)||dt.
```

At the endpoint, `E_int<=eta/32` gives trace error at most `eta`. With a window, the same allocation additionally requires `lambda b w+E_int<=eta/32`. The root endpoint allowance similarly converts to at most twice its coherent error, with window and defect integrals added before conversion. These are upper bounds for the specified sufficient choices, not every arbitrarily oversized repetition count or recurrence search ceiling.

For a finite target product in the root contract, compose augmented pairs approximating `(exp Q_j,I)` in the chosen product order, sum pair errors and actual durations, and only then reconstruct the final background-aged endpoint. Multiplying separate endpoint formulas as though the intermediate `H` flows commute with the targets would give the wrong operation. For a common fixed baseline, stage `j` has smoothed plant error at most `6eta_j` and aging-coordinate error at most `5eta_j`, hence the final bound is `11 sum eta_j`. Actual durations, scalar areas, variations and integrated defects sum; peak field and slew use the actual maxima. A changed baseline needs its own chronological contract. This qualification was recorded in the root's pre-exposure readout and proved explicitly in the exposed comparison; it is current publication interpretation.

## 4. Full physical ledger and calibration

The physical scalar rate is `h0+R_s+lambda j0+g f(t)`. Scalar action, coherent phase, full operator norm, local positive-block sum and state energy mean are different ledgers. The path's `L_P-1` blocks have norm `2lambda` and four Pauli coefficients of magnitude `lambda/2` per edge including the identity; the maximum added incident path load is `4lambda`.

The full nominal norm is at most `h+R_s+lambda j+2g`. Added norm action is at most `(R_s+lambda j)(T+w)+2A_s`; scalar added action is exactly `(R_s+lambda j0)(T+w)+A_s`. Port variation is `4gN_a`, where `N_a` counts active pulses; peak port norm is at most `2g`. Cubic ramps give peak slew at most `3g` divided by the physical ramp width. Recurrence waits contribute their entire time, static action and phase.

The full-space actual-minus-nominal defect `E(t)` includes old-background error, scalar error, path calibration, timing discrepancy and every undeclared coupling. Dynamics cost its norm integral, including the complete retained Hilbert space. A constant rate ceiling must be at most the allocated calibration error divided by `T+w`. At fixed certificate, allocating error proportional to `eta` requires a sufficient rate tolerance scaling like `eta^(P+1)` for `P=ell+2d(ell+1)`. Input approximation costs enter once by contractivity. Classical waveform design is completed before declared physical execution; any plant aging during that design must be separately included.

Robust positivity also needs a finite peak defect bound: choose `R_s>=h+zeta_pk`. An integral alone supplies no peak guarantee. A consumer requiring each inherited local block to be positive must supply its literal decomposition and individual reserves `r_alpha>=||H_alpha||`; replacing the common reserve by their sum changes the scalar, phase, norm and action. The optional termwise construction is a new supplied channel contract, not a consequence of whole-generator positivity.

For regular nominal closed evolution, zero endpoint port control and `B=H+R_sI+lambda J` give

```
W_nom=Tr B[rho_nom(T)-rho_0],
|W_nom|<=min(4gN_a,2h+lambda j).
```

For regular actual dynamics with the same initial state, endpoint fault bounds yield

```
|W_act-W_nom| <= (h+lambda j/2)min(2,2E_int)
                 +||E(T)||+||E(0)||.
```

Integrated dynamical error alone proves neither endpoint work nor positivity. Installation, physical source/actuator manufacture and field-generation work remain separate. A common schedule shift costs at most `4gN_a|Delta t|` at fixed observation time. An actual change of endpoint time requires updating chronological `H` aging and phase or paying the full generator norm times that time change.

For any specified retained Hermitian observable of full norm at most `B_obs` and complete trace error `e`, mean, second-moment and variance errors are bounded by `B_obs e`, `B_obs^2 e`, and `3B_obs^2 e`. Growing Hamiltonian scales must be paid again; small unitary error alone gives no vanishing energy moments.

## 5. Exact scope, witnesses and review record

The theorem is conditional on the full quantitative augmented certificate, computable nominal matrices and target information, supplied positive path and port controls, physical timing and calibration, isolation, and the actual initialization required by any downstream task. It makes no native preparation, unknown-background identification, efficient large-system compiler, common-cap, permanent-stop, reuse or physical-energy-identification claim. No empirical value or fitted target is used to select an answer. Registered units, kinetic-isotropy or realized-state primitives do not supply these coefficients, controls or certificate; no primitive is added or relabeled.

A fixed nonzero `lambda` leaves the explicit window allowance `lambda b w`. Taking `lambda` smaller changes the actual Lie trees/conditioning and all constants unless a new uniform certificate is supplied. On two qubits, `I-SWAP` evolves `|01>` a trace distance `2|sin(lambda s)|`; fixed-certificate endpoint accuracy cannot erase that window motion. The background `H=cI-lambda_*J` can cancel a chosen path at `lambda=lambda_*`; the parent never said every weak coupling works. A scalar terminal spike of height `M` and width `M^-2` has a vanishing integral but unbounded endpoint work. These retained examples reject specific substitutions, not whole research programs.

For `W=W_old tensor I_fillers`, all outputs remain in the ideal target. If `H` acts trivially on fillers their marginal is returned, while their correlations transform with the old system. Reset still requires the separately supplied memory hypothesis on the actually aged input `exp(-iTH)rho exp(iTH)`. Huge compilation time can destroy an initial purity or diagonal promise when `H` couples to the memory. Neither compiler restores or reasserts that resource.

The root proof and protected proof used the same selected model, inherited prior machinery and a shared neutral task with two explicitly identified certificate/window traps. Protection covered exposure to the new root argument, not independence from the parent theorem, model or research question. The later comparison is source-exposed. This publication assembly is a further source-exposed packaging step, with no new decisive mathematical check and no scientific execution. The root chronology readout and protected exposure records remain recoverable. No new literature search or novelty claim is made; historical literature references inside the exact parent remain context only.

