## Immutable source body: root_author

Historical source retained exactly; the current wrapper and separate root decisions govern interpretation.

# Quantitative positive-time compilation with an augmented Lie-basis certificate

This is a proposed conditional sharpening of the finite one-port compiler. It replaces an unbounded word search by an explicit, generally enormous resource recipe when a finite quantitative certificate is supplied. It is not independently checked yet. No physical source, clock state, timing device, unknown-background identification or efficient many-qubit algorithm is supplied by this argument.

## 1. Exact admitted data and target

Use the same fixed plant, old sites, fillers, nearest-neighbor positive path J, one accessible port p, and complete computable Hermitian background H as the accepted single-port compiler source. Every old/filler/reference factor remains. Write H=h0 I+Hbar and J=j0 I+Jbar, with normalized trace defining the scalars. The positive path strength lambda>0 and port amplitude g>0 are supplied at their actual values; Hbar+lambda Jbar is not replaced by a nominal weak-coupling approximation. Let d>=2 be the complete plant dimension, including fillers.

Set A=Hbar+lambda Jbar. In a fixed time unit define the five skew-Hermitian augmented matrices

    X_a=diag(-i(A+v_a), -i Hbar),
    v_a in {0,+g X_p,-g X_p,+g Y_p,-g Y_p}.

The second block is a mathematical record of actual old-background aging, not another physical plant or a freely controllable clock. The norm on augmented matrices is the block operator norm. Supply M>=max_a ||X_a||, M>0. Time units and corresponding Hamiltonian units are held fixed throughout the bounds.

Supply s=d^2-1 formal iterated commutator words B_i in the X_a, each of degree r_i>=2, whose evaluated matrices are diag(B_i^P,0). Their first blocks form a real basis of su(d). Degree is the total number of primitive symbols, not nesting depth. Every degree>=2 commutator has zero second block because all second primitive blocks coincide. A certified sigma>0 lower-bounds the smallest singular value of the s-column real coordinate matrix in a Frobenius-orthonormal basis of su(d). Supply computable upper bounds b_i>=||B_i^P|| and b_i>0.

This certificate is stronger than merely asserting full controllability in the first block. For a valid finite Lie-generating system such words exist: the derived Lie algebra projects onto [su(d),su(d)]=su(d), while its second coordinate is zero. This existence observation gives neither a usable sigma nor uniform word lengths. The theorem below consumes the actual finite words and sigma; it does not replace them by an unquantified density statement.

Supply a computable skew-Hermitian traceless Q with ||Q||_F<=L_Q and a scalar theta such that the target W=e^{i theta} e^Q. A supplied finite product of such exponentials can be handled by repeated invocation with allocated errors and all durations charged. This version does not bound the work of producing a logarithm/circuit for an arbitrary target description. For the inherited preparation use, W is the specified full-plant target, identity on fillers where required. Take the certified bounds M, sigma, b_i and L_Q to be rational; loosening valid computable bounds to positive rational certificates is allowed and charged.

Fix a rational 0<epsilon<=1. Set eta=epsilon/16, B=sum_i b_i, C=1+L_Q/sigma, K=C B. Constants in this statement depend on the actual certificate, target bound, d, H, lambda, g, and time unit. They are not uniform in these data.

## 2. Rational coefficient selection and why small pulses are still priced

Write Q=sum_i c_i^* B_i^P. The real coefficient vector has Euclidean norm <=L_Q/sigma. Choose a dyadic rational delta satisfying

    eta/[2(1+B)] < delta <= eta/(1+B).

Such a number exists. Compute each c_i^* to certified error at most delta/2 and round that approximation to the nearest multiple of delta. The resulting rational c_i satisfies |c_i-c_i^*|<=delta and |c_i|<=C. Consequently

    Q_c=sum_i c_i B_i^P,
    ||Q_c-Q|| <= delta B <= eta,
    ||e^{Q_c}-e^Q|| <= eta.

The last inequality follows by integrating the difference of two unitary flows. Every nonzero c_i has |c_i|>=delta. Zero rational coefficients can be omitted without an undecidable zero test on the original computable real. This lower bound is useful when pricing smooth ramps, not just the total pulse count.

Computability of the basis and the supplied positive sigma makes this finite linear solve and coefficient certification possible. No uniform bit-complexity bound for arbitrary computable-real input oracles is inferred.

## 3. A complete signed word for each bracket, with a computable remainder

For a primitive symbol use W_X(t)=e^{tX}. Recursively define

    W_[U,V](t)=W_U(t) W_V(t) W_U(t)^-1 W_V(t)^-1.

The inverse is implemented algebraically by reversing the list and negating each primitive duration. At this stage signed durations are a mathematical intermediate. Products are written in matrix order; the actual chronological list applies the rightmost factor first.

For a word B_i of degree r_i, let n_i be the number of primitive exponential occurrences in this recursive group word. The formal Taylor coefficients satisfy

    W_i(t)=I+t^{r_i} diag(B_i^P,0)+O(t^{r_i+1}).

Here is a direct finite-series justification. A primitive word has the stated first coefficient. If U=I+t^r U0+O(t^{r+1}) and V=I+t^q V0+O(t^{q+1}), multiplication by their exact inverses cancels all coefficients below r+q in UVU^-1V^-1; its degree r+q term is U0V0-V0U0. Terms involving a higher coefficient have at least one extra power. Induction proves the displayed identity, including unequal bracket degrees. The inverses are analytic products of signed primitive exponentials, so this formal coefficient calculation concerns actual convergent series.

Let S_i=n_i M. The norm of the degree-k Taylor coefficient of a product of n_i signed exponentials is at most S_i^k/k!: expand each exponential, apply submultiplicativity, and use the multinomial identity. Thus for 0<=t<=1, its tail above degree r_i is bounded by

    exp(S_i) S_i^{r_i+1} t^{r_i+1}/(r_i+1)!.

The tail of exp(t^{r_i} B_i) above its linear B_i term is at most (b_i^2 exp(b_i)/2)t^{2r_i}, hence at most that constant times t^{r_i+1}. Compute a positive rational majorant

    E_i>=exp(S_i) S_i^{r_i+1}/(r_i+1)! + b_i^2 exp(b_i)/2.

For instance a convergent certified exponential series supplies a rational upper bound within an additive one of this positive expression. All repetition-count inputs below are then rational, so their ceilings require no equality test on a general computable real.

It follows that

    ||W_i(t)-exp(t^{r_i} diag(B_i^P,0))|| <= E_i t^{r_i+1}.

The same bound holds for the inverse word and the negative exponential, because inverse unitary matrices preserve the norm difference. These very loose constants are genuine bounds; they are not physical efficient-control claims.

## 4. Splitting, repetition and explicit signed length

Let r=max_i r_i, N=sum_i n_i, and D=sum_i E_i C^2. Choose the actual integer

    m=ceil(max(1,C,K^2/eta,(D/eta)^r)).

For each nonzero c_i put t_i=(|c_i|/m)^{1/r_i}<=1. Use W_i(t_i) or its inverse according to the sign of c_i. Their product, repeated m times in the consistent order, approximates exp(diag(Q_c,0)).

For completeness, first compare the exact product of exp(c_i B_i/m) to exp(Q_c/m). For two skew-Hermitian generators U,V, unitary variation of constants gives the local Lie-product error at most ||[U,V]||/(2m^2). Iterating the split and using ||[U,V]||<=2||U||||V|| gives a per-cycle bound no larger than K^2/m^2. Telescoping m unitary cycles gives at most K^2/m<=eta. This argument uses unitary norms, not an exponentially growing nonunitary estimate.

Replacing the exact factors by the bracket words costs at most

    sum_i m E_i (|c_i|/m)^{1+1/r_i}
       <= D m^{-1/r} <= eta.

The inequality uses m>=1, r_i<=r, C>=1 and |c_i|<=C. The full signed list therefore approximates diag(e^Q,I) with error at most 3eta, including coefficient rounding. Its primitive segment count L satisfies L<=mN. Every nonzero primitive duration has magnitude t_i between delta/m and 1. The lower estimate follows from |c_i|>=delta and x^{1/r_i}>=x for 0<x<=1.

If all rounded coefficients vanish, the empty schedule already approximates the target with error <=eta. Treat that case separately with duration zero and no smoothing. All subsequent formulas concern L>=1. No basis-clock theorem requiring a strictly positive runtime is invoked for the empty schedule.

## 5. Positive-time replacement with an explicit recurrence ceiling

Choose the integer q=ceil(16L/eta), which is at least 4 pi L/eta. For any primitive X_a, unitary diagonalization has at most 2d eigenphases. Partition the 2d-dimensional unit cube into q^{2d} equal half-open boxes, and consider the q^{2d}+1 phase vectors of e^{2jX_a}, j=0,...,q^{2d}. Two vectors share a box. Subtracting their indices proves that for some integer 1<=k_a<=q^{2d},

    ||exp(2k_a X_a)-I|| <= 2pi/q <= eta/(2L).

This proof allows degeneracies and irrationally related eigenvalues. It requires no known period and no spectral gap. The dimension 2d, not d, accounts for the actual-aging coordinate as well as the plant.

A finite effective search can find k_a with certified norm strictly below eta/L: inspect the finite candidate list using matrix-exponential/norm enclosures of error less than eta/(4L). At least one candidate has the stated strict margin. One can use certified matrix series/norm approximation instead of eigenvalue calculations. The size of this finite search is explicit, although arbitrary input-oracle bit costs remain excluded.

Replace each negative occurrence exp(-t_i X_a) by exp((2k_a-t_i)X_a). Its new duration is at least 1 because t_i<=1. Its augmented error is at most eta/L. The total replacement error is <=eta by unitary telescoping. Positive occurrences stay unchanged. The positive list then has error <=4eta from diag(e^Q,I), still L segments, and total duration at most

    T_pre <= 2L q^{2d}.

Each negative direction is thus replaced by an actual long positive physical pulse; it is not implemented by an illicit sign reversal of time or of the whole background. The long waits contribute to old aging, action and calibration precision.

For rational durations, replace every positive duration u_j by a positive rational u'_j with

    |u'_j-u_j| <= min(u_j/2, eta/(2ML)).

The augmented error is at most eta/2, in particular <=eta. All durations remain at least delta/(2m), and total actual duration satisfies

    T=sum_j u'_j <= 3L q^{2d} <= 4L q^{2d}.

Both blocks of the actual rational schedule accumulate this new T. Nothing compares its output to the old pre-rounding duration. Its augmented error to diag(e^Q,I) is at most 5eta.

## 6. Same-duration smooth positive one-port controls and the complete endpoint

For each active segment select

    rho_j=min(u'_j/4, eta/(gL)).

If computable rather than rational rho_j is used, it is allowed by the waveform contract; a rational choice between half this value and this value also works, with the lower slew bound below reduced by a factor two. Use the cubic smoothstep 3z^2-2z^3 on the initial/final intervals rho_j and a unit plateau between them. The envelope is C1, with zero derivative at all joins. It occupies exactly the same duration u'_j and is zero at each segment boundary. Zero-control segments require no envelope.

The lost area of each two-ramp envelope is rho_j. The traceless plant perturbation therefore has integrated norm at most g sum_active rho_j<=eta. The second aging coordinate still evolves for exactly T. Thus, writing U_c for the traceless plant propagator, triangle bounds give

    ||U_c(T)-e^Q exp(-i T Hbar)|| <= 2(5eta)+eta
                                          =11eta < epsilon.

The first 5eta bounds the plant block's error from e^Q, the second bounds the old-background block's error from identity, and the final eta is smoothing. This explicitly addresses the moving-target problem; first-factor controllability alone would not.

The physical control is C(t)=g f_j(t)(I+sign_j P_j), P_j=X_p or Y_p, on an active segment; it is zero otherwise. It is positive and entirely onsite at p. The full generator is

    H_phys(t)=H+lambda J+r0 I+C(t).

Here r0>=h+zeta_peak is a supplied physical reserve if ||H||<=h and an actual peak fault zeta_peak must be covered. With no faults r0>=h suffices. It may be placed at p; its scalar is not removed from the ledger. Whole-generator positivity does not by itself provide a positive decomposition of every inherited old local block.

Define A_s=g sum_active(u'_j-rho_j), the exact pulse scalar action, and

    chi(T)=r0 T+lambda j0 T+A_s+theta.

Then the actual ideal endpoint satisfies

    ||U_phys(T)-exp(-i chi(T)) W exp(-i T H)|| < epsilon.

Every scalar and the literal old H evolution remain. Tensoring an arbitrary passive reference and converting the isometry error gives unhalved trace/diamond allowance at most min(2,2epsilon), with every plant/filler/reference factor retained. No fresh ancilla, reset, state discrimination or marginal discard enters this compiler theorem.

If controls are zero on a supplied subsequent interval [T,T+w], retain the installed lambda J and compare to the same background-aged target. The inherited full-space Duhamel estimate adds lambda ||Jbar|| w to the isometry error; chi acquires (r0+lambda j0)w with the actual time. Choosing lambda to make this arbitrarily small changes the certificate and its costs. There is no uniform-in-lambda conclusion here.

## 7. Duration, slope, action, work, calibration and the honest polynomial statement

For the exact rho_j above,

    rho_j >= rho_min=min(delta/(8m), eta/(gL)).

The full physical control has derivative norm at most 3g/rho_min because the cubic envelope has slope at most 3/(2rho_j) and ||I+sign P||=2. For the optional rational rho_j chosen within a factor two, use 6g/rho_min. This is a supplied field slew requirement, not hardware provided by a mathematical waveform.

The complete pulse variation is at most 4gL. A constant background and static reserve do no explicit parameter work during the schedule, so for ideal closed evolution the absolute controlled work is bounded by this variation. Installation, source preparation and field generation costs are separate. A uniform norm allowance B_phys=h+lambda||J||+r0+2g bounds the full action by B_phys(T+w). The exact scalar rate is h0+lambda j0+r0+g f_j, and its integrated scalar, including waits, is retained above.

An actual full-space generator error D(t) adds integral||D(t)||dt to the coherent error and twice that to the complete trace allowance. A constant error ceiling must decrease as the allowed error divided by T+w; long recurrence is not free. Endpoint timing error contributes at most the actual full generator norm times its absolute timing error. Faults are charged on the complete Hilbert space, not only an ideal controller sector.

For a comparison-state trace error e and a supplied full observable norm B_obs, mean, second-moment and variance errors are at most B_obs e, B_obs^2 e and 3B_obs^2 e. The small compilation norm error does not by itself establish vanishing moments for growing energy scales. The pulse work, physical scalar and state energy mean are different quantities.

For fixed admitted certificate and supplied target bound, use the specified q=ceil(16L/eta). With r fixed,

    m=O(epsilon^-r),
    L=O(epsilon^-r),
    q=O(epsilon^-(r+1)),
    T=O(epsilon^-[r+2d(r+1)]),
    rho_min^-1=O(epsilon^-(r+1)).

These powers follow from the specified sufficient choices, not every arbitrarily oversized m or q. Constants include E_i, sigma^-1, M, L_Q, g and the complete word list, and can be enormous. The recurrence search has at most q^{2d} candidates per primitive type. This is a finite quantitative physical recipe and a bound on that finite candidate count. It is not a uniform polynomial algorithm in plant qubit count (d is exponential in it), certificate length, shrinking lambda, inverse conditioning, target-description length or arbitrary real-oracle precision cost.

The physical norm can remain fixed for a fixed certificate while duration, action and slew grow. Composing this waveform with a separately checked autonomous clock changes its duration, Lipschitz and controller-resource inputs; those new costs must all be recomputed. No efficient complete autonomous preparation pipeline is inferred by composition alone.

## 8. What remains unresolved, failures excluded and evidence

The argument does not certify a native supplier of H, J, lambda, one-port field shape, precision, timing, pure/thermal source states, classical detector or controller reset. It does not provide physical energy identification, finite common hardware caps, permanent stopping or reuse. It retains the old compiler's exact geometry and complete computational background premises.

A first-factor Lie basis without zero aging block is insufficient for this construction. A qualitative nonzero determinant without a supplied lower conditioning bound is insufficient for the printed resource constants. An arbitrarily oversized repetition count or recurrence ceiling destroys the stated upper recipe. Ignoring the negative-time replacement, its actual elapsed T, or smoothing duration changes would invalidate the endpoint. Shrinking lambda for a fixed finite observation window may make sigma deteriorate; this proof does not suppress that dependence. These are contract failures and narrow proof boundaries, not general no-go claims.

