# An explicit positive-duration compiler from an augmented Lie-basis certificate

This is a protected analytical derivation prepared before opening, listing, hashing or searching any new root conditioned-compiler candidate. The existing compiler source bda0be88 and its separate review 3ad0ab65 are the mathematical premises; their qualifications are retained. The selection memo and root's neutral request supplied the research question, including the need for a quantitative augmented certificate and the warning about a changing weak-path strength. Those exposures are not independence from the prior machinery. No scientific program, numerical search or concrete pulse instance was run.

The result below is positive and conditional. For a fixed finite admitted certificate it gives explicit polynomial upper recipes in inverse approximation tolerance for a positive-duration word, its duration and its smoothing prices. The exponent is enormous. It does not give a polynomial bound in qubit number, a uniform result over deteriorating certificates, a Turing runtime bound for arbitrary computable-real oracles, a prescribed completion time, native control manufacture, a prepared quantum controller, or memory supply. All outputs of the supplied plant are retained.

## 1. Physical and certificate inputs

Use one fixed nonempty finite plant P of d>=2 dimensions, including all original factors and all added dirty fillers. A passive reference R may have arbitrary dimension and arbitrary correlations with P. Every old site stays at its original position. The accepted filled-box positive NN path has

    J=sum_edges(I-SWAP),     0<=J<=j I,
    j=2(L_P-1),             j0=Tr(J)/d=(L_P-1)/2,
    Jbar=J-j0 I,            ||Jbar||<=b=3(L_P-1)/2.

Here L_P is the number of qubits on that path and d=2^(L_P) in that application. The proof also works for any finite supplied J with these declared bounds and the certificate below. Complete computable matrices and local coefficients of H and J are supplied. H is the literal unchanged complete background, including original H0 and every installed term named for this invocation; h>=||H|| is a certified bound. Write h0=Tr(H)/d and Hbar=H-h0 I. Neither h0 nor H0 is silently dropped.

Fix lambda>0, g>0 and a physical time unit t0>0. Set

    A=Hbar+lambda Jbar,
    v_i in {0,+gX_p,-gX_p,+gY_p,-gY_p},
    X_i=diag(-i t0(A+v_i), -i t0 Hbar),     i=1,...,5.       (1)

These are skew-Hermitian matrices on a mathematical direct sum of dimension D=2d. The second block records actual elapsed background time. It is not a physical register or an omitted output. A physical constant segment of duration t0 u realizes exp(u X_i) in this bookkeeping system after removing its explicitly retained identity coefficients.

Supply a rational M>=1 bounding every ||X_i||. Supply s=d^2-1 binary commutator trees T_l in the symbols X_i, each with leaf count ell_l>=2, whose evaluations are

    B_l=diag(b_l,0),   b_l in su(d),   l=1,...,s,             (2)

and whose first blocks form a real basis of su(d). Every tree of length at least two has second block exactly zero, since all second leaf blocks in (1) are identical and commute. This is an algebraic assertion, not a near-zero numerical test. The certificate also supplies a rational kappa>=1 such that the coordinates of every Z in su(d) obey

    Z=sum_l c_l b_l  ==>  sum_l |c_l| <= kappa ||Z||.        (3)

For example, express b_l in a fixed Hilbert-Schmidt orthonormal real basis of su(d). If the resulting s by s real matrix has certified smallest singular value at least sigma>0, then kappa>=sqrt(sd)/sigma suffices, since ||Z||_F<=sqrt(d)||Z|| and ||c||_1<=sqrt(s)||c||_2. The matrices are full plant matrices, not excitation-sector projections. A certificate may be verified by sufficiently accurate interval matrix arithmetic; verification and manufacture are not free physical operations supplied by this theorem.

The original qualitative controllability theorem implies existence of some such finite list for an admitted lambda. Indeed the Lie algebra generated by (1) projects onto su(d). The kernel of its second projection contains the port-axis differences and is an ideal under that projected algebra; simplicity gives (su(d),0). Its derived algebra is spanned by commutator monomials of length at least two. A finite basis can therefore be selected. This existence observation does not supply a uniform tree depth, a lower singular-value bound or a cost of discovering them. The theorem here takes the actual quantitative list and (3) as inputs.

Supply a computable unitary W on the complete plant and a computable determinant lift theta such that Wtilde=exp(-i theta) W belongs to SU(d). In the accepted application W is W_old tensor I_fillers, or an explicitly declared full target. Supply rational construction tolerance 0<eta<=1 and, optionally, a finite window w>=0. Exact equality promises about unitarity and the determinant lift are input contracts. No matrix-logarithm branch, target Lie coordinates or pure ancillary state is assumed.

## 2. A finite target search without a logarithm oracle

Every U in SU(d) has a traceless skew-Hermitian logarithm Z with

    exp(Z)=U,       ||Z||<=pi(d+1)<4(d+1).                  (4)

To see this, diagonalize U with eigenangles in (-pi,pi]. Their sum is 2pi k for an integer k with |k|<=d/2. Subtract 2pi k from one angle. The altered angles sum to zero, their exponentials are unchanged, and their magnitudes are at most pi(d+1). Conjugating the diagonal skew matrix proves existence. This step is not an algorithm for selecting eigenangle branches of a general computable input.

Define the certificate constants

    beta_l=2^(ell_l-1) M^(ell_l),
    Bsum=sum_l beta_l,
    R0=4 kappa(d+1),
    K0=s(R0+2),                K=1+K0.                     (5)

Repeated ||[X,Y]||<=2||X||||Y|| gives ||B_l||<=beta_l. By (3)-(4), at least one logarithm of Wtilde has every coordinate in [-R0,R0]. Put

    alpha=eta/(64 d Bsum),
    m_grid=ceil(R0/alpha)+1.

Enumerate the finite grid c_l=k_l alpha with integer |k_l|<=m_grid. For each grid point compute a certified upper Frobenius-norm bound, exceeding the true value by at most eta/256, for

    exp(sum_l c_l b_l)-Wtilde.

Accept a point with certified bound strictly below eta/32; otherwise continue to the next point. A witness exists with strict margin. Round the coordinates of a logarithm from (4) to the grid. The matrix error is at most alpha Bsum; exponential Duhamel for skew-Hermitian matrices gives operator error at most that amount and Frobenius error at most sqrt(d) alpha Bsum<=eta/64. The stated fixed enclosure accuracy makes that witness pass. No individual failed candidate is refined indefinitely. The search finds a point among at most

    (2 m_grid+1)^s                                               (6)

candidates. Exact zero tests, spectral branch selection and a continuous choice of logarithm are unnecessary. Since alpha<=1, every grid coordinate satisfies |c_l|<=R0+2, and hence sum |c_l|<=K0. Write Z_g=sum c_l b_l for the selected matrix. Then

    ||exp(Z_g)-Wtilde||<eta/32.                              (7)

The grid bound is polynomial in 1/eta at fixed certificate and dimension. This is a bound on the finite candidate set, not on the time taken by arbitrary computable-real oracles to supply the needed digits. Complete nominal matrix data remain supplied.

## 3. Quantitative commutator words from Taylor jets

For each leaf X_i define the signed word W_i(u)=exp(u X_i), with length k_i=1. Recursively define

    W_[a,b](u)=W_a(u) W_b(u) W_a(u)^(-1) W_b(u)^(-1),
    k_[a,b]=2(k_a+k_b).                                     (8)

An inverse means reversed factor order with all signs reversed at this stage. Physical negative times have not yet been authorized. These are algebraic signed words. Let k_l be the exact length computed from T_l and ell_l its leaf count. Induction gives

    W_l(u)=I+u^(ell_l) B_l+O(u^(ell_l+1)).                  (9)

For completeness, if F=I+u^a A+O(u^(a+1)) and G=I+u^b B+O(u^(b+1)), then

    FGF^(-1)G^(-1)-I=(FG-GF)F^(-1)G^(-1)
                     =u^(a+b)[A,B]+O(u^(a+b+1)).

This proves both the sign in (8) and the vanishing of all lower Taylor coefficients. It does not assume the subwords commute.

For any real u the factors in W_l(u) are unitary. The Leibniz formula therefore bounds its mth derivative by (k_l M)^m: the multinomial sum of the derivative norms is the mth power of the sum of the leaf norm bounds. Taylor's integral remainder, together with (9), gives

    ||W_l(u)-I-u^(ell_l)B_l||
       <= (k_l M)^(ell_l+1) |u|^(ell_l+1)/(ell_l+1)!.

For 0<=u<=1, the unitary exponential's second-order remainder is at most beta_l^2 u^(2ell_l)/2. Since 2ell_l>=ell_l+1, define

    a_l=(k_l M)^(ell_l+1)/(ell_l+1)! + beta_l^2/2

to obtain the explicit bound

    ||W_l(u)-exp(u^(ell_l) B_l)|| <= a_l u^(ell_l+1).      (10)

The inverse word satisfies the same bound for exp(-u^(ell_l)B_l), by unitary invariance. No unbounded BCH remainder or asymptotic-only step is used. All constants are computable from the supplied finite trees and norm certificate.

Each tree word with ell_l>=2 has zero signed total duration: (8) contains every subword and its inverse. It also has zero signed count for each individual generator. The same is true after taking its inverse. This exact balance will keep the chronology explicit after positive-time replacement.

## 4. A finite signed approximation with explicit length

Avoid deciding the sign or exact vanishing of a computable target coefficient. Replace each c_l B_l by two terms

    a_l^+ B_l + a_l^-(-B_l),
    a_l^+=(K+c_l)/2,        a_l^-=(K-c_l)/2.                (11)

Here the a_l^+/- notation is distinct from the remainder constant a_l in (10). Both weights lie in [1/2,K], and their sum is K. The selected c_l are rational, so these are in fact rational weights. Let

    ell=max_l ell_l,
    S=K Bsum,
    C=2 K^2 sum_l a_l,
    Q_word=2 sum_l k_l.

Choose exactly the finite sufficient integer

    r=ceil(max{1, 2K, 8 S^2/eta, (16 C/eta)^ell}).        (12)

For each of the 2s signed basis terms use the corresponding W_l or W_l^(-1), at

    u_l^+/-=(a_l^+/- / r)^(1/ell_l).

These numbers satisfy

    1/(2r)<=u_l^+/-<=1.                                    (13)

Repeat the ordered product of these 2s words exactly r times. Its number of elementary signed factors is

    N=Q_word r.                                            (14)

The order of the first-block target factors is fixed once; no commuting simplification is made. The first-order product formula for skew-Hermitian C_j obeys

    ||(product_j exp(C_j/r))^r-exp(sum_j C_j)||
       <= (1/(2r)) sum_(i<j)||[C_i,C_j]||
       <= S^2/(2r).                                      (15)

One proof differentiates the ordered product at parameter t, compares its left logarithmic derivative with sum C_j, and bounds each conjugation difference by t||[C_i,C_j]||. Integrating t from 0 to 1/r gives the first factor 1/(2r^2); telescoping r unitary products gives (15). The commutator sum is bounded by 2 sum_(i<j)||C_i||||C_j||<=S^2. This bound is valid without mutual commutation.

Using (10), the error of replacing each small exponential by its signed word and repeating is at most

    sum_(l,+/-) a_l (a_l^+/-)^(1+1/ell_l) r^(-1/ell_l)
       <= C r^(-1/ell).

Each of (15) and this last bound is at most eta/16 by (12). Thus the signed augmented word U_signed obeys

    ||U_signed-diag(exp(Z_g),I)||<=eta/8.                  (16)

Its second block is exactly I, because its signed total duration is exactly zero. The looser joint bound (16) is convenient for subsequent accounting. No physical trajectory with negative time has been claimed.

## 5. Bounded simultaneous recurrence replaces every inverse

Set

    delta=eta/(16N),
    Q=ceil(32D/delta),       D=2d.                         (17)

For each of the five X_i there exists an integer

    1<=q_i<=Q^D

with

    ||exp(2 q_i X_i)-I||_F<delta/4.                       (18)

Indeed, write the D eigenvalues of X_i as i omega_j. Put the Q^D+1 points whose coordinates are the fractional parts of 2k omega_j/(2pi), k=0,...,Q^D, into Q^D boxes of side 1/Q. A pair in one box has difference q_i between 1 and Q^D, and all D eigenphases are within 2pi/Q of multiples of 2pi. Hence the Frobenius distance is at most 2pi sqrt(D)/Q<delta/4. Degenerate, rationally related, zero and irrational frequencies all satisfy this argument; no spectral gap or known common recurrence period is used.

To select q_i, enumerate this finite integer range and compute a certified upper Frobenius-norm bound exceeding the true value by at most delta/16. Accept a value whose bound is below delta/2; otherwise continue to the next integer without an exact-threshold test. A strict witness from (18) passes at this fixed enclosure accuracy. The accepted q_i has operator error below delta/2, which we conservatively price as delta. Eigenvalues need not actually be calculated: certified finite matrix exponential approximation suffices. The larger factor D in (17) deliberately makes the Frobenius acceptance test, rather than an unimplemented operator-norm oracle, sufficient.

An elementary negative factor exp(-u X_i) is replaced by

    exp((2q_i-u) X_i),                                    (19)

at operator cost at most delta. Its physical duration is t0(2q_i-u)>=t0>0. An elementary positive factor retains duration t0 u>0. These are actual allowed positive-time segments. The same q_i can be reused for every inverse of generator i. Product telescoping costs at most N delta=eta/16, so the positive augmented word U_pc obeys

    ||U_pc-diag(exp(Z_g),I)||<=3eta/16.                    (20)

The matrices in (8)-(20) use algebraic product order. Execute the elementary factors in reverse order to obtain that product under the conventional chronological propagator. Reversal changes none of the lengths, durations or estimates.

Let T be the sum of all positive physical durations. Then

    t_min>=t0/(2r),
    T<=2t0 N Q^D.                                         (21)

More exactly, signed balance gives T=2t0 sum_negative_factors q_i. This is an actual positive elapsed time, not a reset of the mathematical clock. The second block of the positive word is precisely exp(-i T Hbar). Joint recurrence in (18) includes this block. It cannot be replaced by recurrence of the plant block alone.

From (7) and (20), the first block differs from Wtilde by at most 7eta/32, while the second differs from I by at most 3eta/16. Therefore

    ||U_pc,plant(T)-Wtilde exp(-i T Hbar)||<=13eta/32.      (22)

The actual drift A was present during every positive segment and every long recurrence wait. There is no lambda T smallness assumption. The construction chooses its own T; it does not solve arbitrary prescribed-time control.

## 6. Positive C1 port pulses at exactly the same duration

Only nonzero-control segments need smoothing. Let N_a<=N be their number and define the common dimensionless ramp width

    rho=min{1/(8r), eta/(16 t0 g N)}.                       (23)

Since each segment duration is at least t0/(2r), two ramps of physical width t0 rho fit with room for a plateau. On an active segment with v_i=sigma g P, P=X_p or Y_p, use the cubic q(x)=3x^2-2x^3 for the rising ramp, a unit plateau, and its reversed falling ramp. The physical control is

    C(t)=g f(t)(I+sigma P)>=0.                             (24)

Controls vanish at every segment boundary with zero derivative, so the concatenation is C1 and has the same total physical duration T. There is no appended settling interval. The entire [T,T+w] window has zero control.

The area lost from each active rectangular traceless pulse is exactly t0 rho. Duhamel bounds the first-block smoothing error by g t0 N_a rho<=eta/16. Keep the actual positive pulse's scalar area separately:

    A_s=g sum_active(t_l-t0 rho).

Thus the smoothed traceless plant propagator satisfies

    ||U_sm(T)-Wtilde exp(-i T Hbar)||<=15eta/32.            (25)

Let R_s>=h be a supplied constant scalar reserve. The nominal physical generator is

    H_ph(t)=H+R_s I+lambda J+C(t).                         (26)

It is positive on the entire plant space. The port pulses and each added path block are separately positive. Whole-generator positivity does not make each literal old local channel separately positive; section 8 states that stronger optional contract and its extra prices.

The physical coherent phase is exactly

    chi(T+s)=(R_s+lambda j0)(T+s)+A_s+theta.

Restoring the h0 scalar already included in exp(-iTH), and then using Duhamel only over the post-endpoint window, yields

    sup_(0<=s<=w) ||U_ph(T+s)
      -exp(-i chi(T+s)) exp(-isH) W exp(-iTH)||
       <=15eta/32+lambda b w.                              (27)

The scalar phase is not required to recur. It is explicitly retained with its actual area. The original H0 is included in the literal H on both sides; H need not commute with W or any pulse. The reference tensor factor is the identity throughout.

For any joint plant/reference density and any compatible actual-minus-nominal full-space generator defect E(t), let E_int=int_0^(T+w)||E(t)||dt. Then the complete unhalved trace-distance bound is

    min{2, 2[15eta/32+lambda b w+E_int]}.                  (28)

No dimension factor is added by the reference or by tracing no outputs. This follows by expanding U rho U* minus V rho V* into two products and using trace/operator norm duality. Every old factor, filler and stored record remains in the target. A separately supplied complete input error adds once by contractivity.

In particular, at the endpoint w=0, choosing E_int<=eta/32 gives complete unhalved trace error at most eta. With a window the same conclusion requires lambda b w+E_int<=eta/32. This latter allocation does not itself give a uniformly conditioned certificate as lambda changes.

## 7. Explicit polynomial upper recipes and their domain

All constants below depend only on the fixed admitted certificate, t0, g, d and the supplied norm/conditioning bounds. Define

    C_r=1+2K+8S^2+(16C)^ell,
    C_N=Q_word C_r,
    C_Q=1+512D C_N,
    P=ell+D(ell+1)=ell+2d(ell+1).

For 0<eta<=1, (12), (14), (17) and (21) imply

    r<=C_r eta^(-ell),
    N<=C_N eta^(-ell),
    Q<=C_Q eta^(-(ell+1)),
    T<=2t0 C_N C_Q^D eta^(-P).                            (29)

These are sufficient upper bounds for the explicit choices, not bounds on every longer word that also attains the tolerance. The target-grid count in (6) is O(eta^(-s)); each of the five recurrence searches has at most Q^D candidates. Neither search is an unbounded semigroup enumeration.

The inverse physical ramp width obeys

    1/(t0 rho)
      <=(8C_r/t0+16g C_N) eta^(-(ell+1)).                  (30)

The peak port norm is at most 2g, peak port slew at most 3g/(t0 rho), and port variation is exactly 4gN_a. Their sufficient bounds therefore have the displayed polynomial dependence. The static drift and all scalar reserves persist for the much longer T. Their action is not bounded by N alone.

Equation (29) does not establish a classical polynomial-time compiler for arbitrary computable inputs. The hypotheses give algorithms producing certified approximations, without a runtime bound on those algorithms. The finite grid and recurrence candidate counts, physical word length and physical duration are separately bounded. The fixed norm-enclosure accuracies above avoid exact equality tests; computing them still invokes the supplied coefficient oracles. For example, recurrence at a candidate q requires correspondingly accurate nominal matrix entries because a matrix error is amplified for time 2q. This is distinct from the actual hardware calibration budget below. If a model charges arithmetic/oracle precision or search labor, its costs must be supplied and added. The waveform is designed before the declared physical execution starts. If the plant instead evolves during that design/search, its extra chronological evolution needs its own contract. This proof does not run either search or certify practical usefulness.

Most importantly, these constants are fixed-certificate constants. If lambda changes with accuracy, the actual trees, beta_l, kappa or their sizes may change. If the output window w>0 is fixed and lambda is fixed, (27) retains the nonzero allowance lambda b w; arbitrary total accuracy is not concluded. To make that allowance shrink with a target tolerance one must supply an accuracy-dependent lambda and separately control the resulting certificate. For example, inverse-polynomial conditioning together with a fixed tree family could lead to a further polynomial recipe after all exponents are recomputed. That is not proved or assumed here. Nonvanishing of a Lie determinant at a chosen lambda is not a lower singular-value estimate uniform in lambda.

Likewise d, ell, kappa, h, g, t0, target-description access and the post-endpoint window cannot silently vary while calling (29) a uniform theorem. In the filled-box application d itself is exponential in the number of qubits and ell may be enormous. No efficient scaling in plant size or a common hardware cap is asserted.

## 8. Physical ledger, calibration, positivity and work

The construction uses the same fixed geometry and single boundary X/Y port as the source theorem. It adds no pure filler, no quantum clock, no new reservoir and no globally driven control. The five alphabet elements differ only by the two port axes. The path, its coefficients, static reserve, timing apparatus, waveform delivery and full isolation are supplied. Exact empty omitted channels are nominal declarations, not demonstrations of native isolation. Every actual unlisted old-old, old-new, new-new and exterior interaction must be included or bounded on the full retained space.

The path has L_P-1 static positive blocks, norm 2lambda each, and four Pauli coefficients per bond of magnitude lambda/2 including the identity. Its maximum added incident block-norm load is 4lambda. The whole generator's identity coefficient at time t is

    h0+R_s+lambda j0+g f(t),

with f=0 on zero-control segments and the window. This coefficient, the coherent phase in (27), the whole norm and the positive-block norm sum are distinct ledgers. In particular

    ||H_ph(t)||<=h+R_s+lambda j+2g,
    added norm action <=(R_s+lambda j)(T+w)+2A_s,
    control norm action =2A_s,
    scalar added action =(R_s+lambda j0)(T+w)+A_s.

The old background adds its own norm/action ledger. Every recurrence wait contributes to time, static action and scalar phase. For fixed supplied values these action bounds are polynomial with exponent P from (29); nothing makes them small.

For a physical defect bound zeta(t)>=||E(t)||, full-space Duhamel uses its integral. A constant rate zeta<=epsilon_cal/(T+w), when T+w>0, gives E_int<=epsilon_cal. Thus the sufficient inverse rate scales at worst with eta^(-(P+1)) if epsilon_cal is proportional to eta. Scalar coefficient error, path strength error, any new boundary edge and the whole unknown background are included. A long recurrence is not robust to an unpriced fixed matrix error.

A common shift Delta t of the control schedule, extended by zero outside [0,T], has integrated discrepancy at most 4gN_a |Delta t| by the variation bound. This is a same-observation-time estimate. If actual endpoint time changes, update H aging and chi or charge the full nominal generator norm times the timing change. Independent duration errors may instead be charged by summing each full segment norm times its error. At fixed certificate a sufficient common timing tolerance proportional to eta/(gN) is polynomially small. Native timing manufacture is not derived.

For robust positivity of the entire actual generator, supply a finite peak defect bound zeta_pk and choose R_s>=h+zeta_pk. An integrated defect allowance alone is insufficient. If a consumer requires every specified old local term H_alpha to be separately positive after reserving scalars, supply its actual finite local decomposition and bounds r_alpha>=||H_alpha||, install H_alpha+r_alpha I on the same declared support, and replace the total reserve by sum r_alpha plus any independently allocated fault reserves. This changes the physical scalar, norm, action and phase ledger. It is not inferred from R_s>=h and does not assert native control of old terms. The port and path blocks already have their displayed positive decompositions.

For regular nominal closed dynamics, C(0)=C(T)=0 and B=H+R_s I+lambda J give the exact formal work identity

    W_nom=int_0^T Tr(rho dot C)dt
         =Tr[B(rho_nom(T)-rho_0)].

Consequently

    |W_nom|<=min{4gN_a, 2h+lambda j}.                      (31)

The scalar reserve cancels from the endpoint difference but not from phase or action. The path endpoint-energy change is included. For regular actual dynamics with the same initial state and defect E, the original review's endpoint argument gives

    |W_act-W_nom|
      <=(h+lambda j/2) min{2,2E_int}
         +||E(T)||+||E(0)||.                              (32)

Endpoint defect bounds therefore suffice; a derivative/variation bound is an alternative for a termwise work estimate. An integrated dynamical allowance alone proves no peak positivity or endpoint work bound. This is finite Hamiltonian bookkeeping, not a derivation of microscopic energy, heat, a bath, Landauer saturation or an actuator's energy supply.

For any selected retained Hermitian observable O with ||O||<=B_O and complete state error e from (28), its mean error is at most B_O e, its second-moment error at most B_O^2 e and its variance error at most 3B_O^2 e. Apply this to the actual specified finite endpoint Hamiltonian only with its full norm, including reserves. There is no vacuum/single-excitation energy formula here: fillers and all plant inputs are arbitrary. If a later autonomous substitution has growing norms, these growing factors must be charged anew.

## 9. Retained-output consequences, failure routes and boundary

For W=W_old tensor I_fillers, the ideal complete output has exactly the old transformation and H aging specified in (27). If H acts trivially on fillers, their marginal is returned; their correlations undergo the intended old transformation. The target is not an assertion that all joint correlation observables remain numerically unchanged. A reset consequence still requires the aged input exp(-iTH)rho exp(iTH) to satisfy the separately supplied memory hypothesis. The potentially huge T can spoil an initial purity or diagonal promise when H couples to that memory. No compiler theorem restores that promise automatically.

The following shortcuts are excluded by concrete mechanisms already visible in the proof or parent review.

* A plant-only recurrence may change the second coordinate and hence the actual-aging target; (18) recurs both full blocks.
* A projected controllability statement gives no quantitative zero-second-coordinate basis. The explicit trees and kappa are indispensable data here.
* H=cI-lambda_* J can cancel the selected path at lambda=lambda_*, leaving only port control and destroying remote controllability. Arbitrarily weak admissible choices in the parent theorem do not make every weak choice valid.
* Formal negative flows in (8) are not physical pulses; all are replaced by (19) and the added duration is paid.
* Choosing any r above a lower bound does not preserve the particular upper recipe (29). Equation (12), or a matching upper choice, is part of the resource statement.
* A fixed nonzero lambda does not give an arbitrarily accurate fixed positive window. On two qubits the positive path I-SWAP moves |01> a trace distance 2|sin(lambda s)| after the endpoint.
* A scalar defect rising to height M in a terminal interval of length M^-2 has vanishing integrated norm but unbounded endpoint work. Conversely a rapidly oscillating scalar with zero endpoint defect can have zero net work despite arbitrarily large derivative. Equation (32) keeps these distinctions.
* A supplied unitary compiler cannot erase arbitrary maximally mixed records, prepare a pure clock, or renew a consumed bank without its separate resource premises.

These are scoped failures of substitutions, not a broad impossibility theorem. The positive construction succeeds at the stated conditional contract. The simpler fixed-certificate endpoint statement is the primary conclusion; varying-lambda window families, explicit physical controller substitution, and any additional source-to-runtime chronology remain separate obligations.

