# Exposed comparison of two conditioned positive-time compiler constructions

## 1. Disposition and exact scope

The root proposal **2de387eb501aa8ead91afa1f5a26f7d3a0bbf11e51285d99786715152ad5b6d6** (18,196 bytes) and the protected derivation **dd6cca8552a117d97f7be21c7b999ecd2276382f6cc762954bd97d00e3a6ff04** (30,870 bytes) support two conditional quantitative compiler recipes. Their commutator, splitting, recurrence, timing, smoothing and full-output calculations hold at the supplied finite augmented-certificate scope. I found no further mathematical repair needed in either immutable proof. The root's two chronology qualifications in readout **d30ed09efe424a00942f79df8c4d94ab4f5a2e82dcf6f4a79a25365628a03048** are mandatory current interpretation and are made explicit below.

The root recipe accepts a supplied traceless logarithm Q, or a finite list of such target factors. The protected recipe accepts a computable SU(d) target with its determinant lift and uses a finite coefficient grid, so it does not require a supplied computable logarithm branch. These are distinct target-data contracts. They share the same type of fixed, quantitatively conditioned basis of (su(d),0), and both have sufficient duration exponent ell+2d(ell+1), where ell is the maximum total leaf count of the supplied commutator trees. This is not an efficient many-qubit compiler or a uniform bound over changing certificates.

The first full exposed read occurred in the tool batch observed at 20:47:22 UTC on 2026-10-15. The protected proof had frozen at 20:44:51.221392 UTC; root's complete pre-exposure read was recorded at 20:47:00.996657 UTC. The root candidate froze at 20:34:18.042746 UTC, before root received the later protected-route outline according to its readout. Root authored that candidate. This report is a source-exposed comparison by the protected proof's author, using the same model/effort and extensive shared earlier context. It is not a third independent derivation, an independent audit or an empirical validation.

No scientific program, target-grid search, recurrence search, matrix fixture, pulse compilation or numerical propagation ran in this comparison. Actual new execution is confined to source/recovery metadata. Original proofs and decisions remain byte-identical.

## 2. Shared hypothesis and target ledger

Both constructions use the original compiler's complete finite nonempty plant, dirty fillers, fixed positive NN path J, supplied complete H, actual lambda>0, actual g>0 and one X/Y port. H includes literal H0 and every other background term declared for this invocation. They do not replace its coefficients by a norm bound. Their five mathematical generators are

    X_a=diag(-i(A+v_a),-iHbar),
    A=Hbar+lambda Jbar,
    v_a in {0,+gX_p,-gX_p,+gY_p,-gY_p}.

The protected proof includes an explicit time unit t0; set that unit to one to compare formulas, without changing physical coefficients. The direct sum has dimension 2d and is bookkeeping, not a second physical plant. All second primitive blocks coincide. Every commutator of degree at least two therefore has an exactly zero second block.

The supplied basis consists of s=d^2-1 actual commutator trees, not merely linearly independent projected control directions. Root uses a lower singular-value certificate sigma in Frobenius coordinates. Protected input uses an operator-norm-to-coordinate bound kappa; kappa>=sqrt(sd)/sigma translates the root certificate into that form. This conversion follows from ||c||_1<=sqrt(s)||c||_2 and ||Z||_F<=sqrt(d)||Z||. It is a bound for the actual admitted matrices and does not provide unknown-background identification or uniformity in lambda.

Both retain the correct coherent endpoint and window targets:

    endpoint:  exp[-i chi(T)] W exp(-iTH),
    window:    exp[-i chi(T+s)] exp(-isH) W exp(-iTH),
               0<=s<=w,
    chi(T+s)=(r0+lambda j0)(T+s)+A_s+theta.                (1)

Here j0=Tr(J)/d, A_s is the actual smoothed pulse scalar area, and theta is the supplied target determinant lift. The physical scalar rate also contains h0=Tr(H)/d; that part is already inside exp(-iTH) and exp(-isH). The lift theta is part of the comparison phase, not an extra Hamiltonian action that was physically applied. The actual scalar action and chi are different quantities.

The complete operator estimates imply twice that error in unhalved trace distance, capped at two, on arbitrary plant/reference inputs. No sector projection, marginal discard or pure filler is used. If H acts trivially on fillers and W is identity there, their marginal is returned; the intended old transformation still changes joint correlation observables. Reset consequences remain conditional on the **aged** input satisfying its separate memory premise. Long compilation time does not preserve an arbitrary initial memory promise when H couples to it.

## 3. Root target rounding and protected finite-grid target

Write the root's internal tolerance as eta_R=epsilon_R/16. Its basis coordinate matrix has smallest singular value at least sigma, so the exact coefficients of the supplied Q obey ||c*||_2<=L_Q/sigma. The dyadic spacing

    eta_R/[2(1+B)]<delta<=eta_R/(1+B),   B=sum b_i,

exists. All interval endpoints are rational certificate data. Approximating each coordinate to delta/2 and rounding to the nearest delta-multiple gives |c_i-c_i*|<=delta and |c_i|<=1+L_Q/sigma=C. Since delta<1, this latter bound is valid even at a rounding tie. Thus ||Q_c-Q||<=delta B<=eta_R and exponential Duhamel gives the same unitary error. Every retained nonzero rational coefficient has magnitude at least delta. Exact equality of a computable real is never decided; only the rounded rational is tested for zero.

A stable finite coefficient solve is justified by the supplied sigma. For example, its positive Gram matrix has a known lower eigenvalue bound sigma^2 and a computable upper bound, so a convergent inverse series with a quantitative ratio below one can certify the required coefficient errors. This is a computability argument, not a polynomial bit-runtime assertion for arbitrary coefficient oracles.

The protected construction instead proves that every U in SU(d) has some traceless skew logarithm of operator norm at most pi(d+1): choose eigenangles in (-pi,pi], then change one by the integer multiple of 2pi needed to make their sum zero. This is an existence lemma, not an algorithm for following a discontinuous eigenangle branch. With the supplied kappa it places at least one logarithm inside a bounded coordinate box. A finite grid with spacing eta_I/(64d Bsum) contains a point whose exponential has Frobenius error at most eta_I/64. A certified upper norm bound with excess at most eta_I/256 makes the eta_I/32 acceptance test pass with strict margin. The finite grid can be inspected without indefinitely refining a candidate exactly on a threshold.

The protected search therefore handles arbitrary computable W with its determinant lift at this fixed basis, without adding a logarithm oracle. It does not make the root's supplied-Q assumption false or unnecessary in that source. Conversely, a finite product of supplied root logarithms is not automatically a supplied single logarithm. Root's direct coordinate solve avoids the protected grid's large finite target-search count; the protected construction has the broader target-description contract. Neither is uniformly cheaper in its printed physical constants.

The protected positive/negative coordinate split uses weights (K+c_i)/2 and (K-c_i)/2, each at least 1/2. It keeps both signs and can execute a large nonempty word even for the identity. Root can omit zero rounded coordinates and correctly has a separate empty-schedule case. If all root coefficients vanish, ||e^Q-I||<=eta_R, T=0 and no smoothing or positive-runtime clock import is needed. The phase convention in (1) still gives the correct target comparison. This distinction is real and should remain visible.

## 4. Bracket remainder and noncommuting splitting

Both sources use the same group-commutator recursion

    W_[U,V](t)=W_U(t) W_V(t) W_U(t)^(-1) W_V(t)^(-1).

The exact identity UVU^(-1)V^(-1)-I=(UV-VU)U^(-1)V^(-1) shows that leading terms t^a U0 and t^b V0 produce t^(a+b)[U0,V0]. Higher terms have at least one more power. This verifies the bracket sign, unequal-degree case and vanishing of all lower Taylor coefficients. Its primitive exponential count obeys n_[U,V]=2(n_U+n_V), not the degree itself. All algebraic products are implemented in reversed chronological order, as both proofs explicitly state.

For root's S_i=n_i M, multiplying exponential series bounds the degree-k coefficient by S_i^k/k!. For 0<=t<=1,

    sum_(k>=r_i+1) S_i^k t^k/k!
      <= exp(S_i) S_i^(r_i+1)t^(r_i+1)/(r_i+1)!.

The exact-exponential remainder is at most b_i^2 exp(b_i)t^(2r_i)/2, and 2r_i>=r_i+1. Thus root's rational E_i majorant is valid, including M below one and unequal degrees. Certified rational upper majorants ensure that its later repetition ceiling does not require an exact real-equality decision.

The protected proof uses the additional fact that all factors remain unitary for real t. A product with n_i factors has kth derivative norm at most (n_i M)^k by the Leibniz multinomial identity. Taylor's integral remainder and the unitary second-order exponential remainder therefore give the smaller valid constant

    E_i,jet=(n_i M)^(r_i+1)/(r_i+1)! + b_i^2/2.             (2)

Equation (2), with an actual b_i bound, is a reusable refinement already present in the protected derivation's norm-bound convention. It is not silently substituted into root's unchanged E_i, m or numerical constants. Root's exponential majorants are loose but sound. No dominance of the entire protected recipe follows, because its coordinate and word choices are larger in other ways.

For skew-Hermitian terms C_i, differentiation of the ordered product and unitary conjugation bounds give per-cycle product error at most (1/(2m^2))sum_(i<j)||[C_i,C_j]||. Using ||[C_i,C_j]||<=2||C_i||||C_j|| bounds this by K^2/(2m^2) when sum ||C_i||<=K. Root uses the looser K^2/m^2, which is safe. Repeating m cycles telescopes the error; there is no assumption that the basis terms or H commute.

Root's bracket replacement contributes

    sum_i E_i |c_i|^(1+1/r_i) m^(-1/r_i)
      <=D m^(-1/r),
    D=sum_i E_i C^2,  r=max r_i,

because C>=1, m>=1 and r_i<=r. Its selected

    m=ceil(max{1,C,K^2/eta_R,(D/eta_R)^r})

makes splitting and bracket error at most eta_R each. Coefficient rounding adds eta_R, giving the stated 3eta_R augmented bound. The same reasoning verifies the protected signed-word budget eta_I/8 with its distinct repetition constant and doubled signed basis list. No error term is missing from either total.

## 5. Simultaneous recurrence, norm enclosures and actual timing

Root sets q=ceil(16L/eta_R), where L is the actual nonempty signed primitive count. Since 16>4pi, its pigeonhole argument on 2d eigenphases gives some 1<=k_a<=q^(2d) with

    ||exp(2k_a X_a)-I||<=2pi/q<=eta_R/(2L).

Degenerate and irrational spectra cause no defect. The exact recurrence is not claimed; the strict margin below the later eta_R/L acceptance threshold is what makes a finite certificate search possible. A certified upper operator-norm enclosure with excess less than eta_R/(4L) makes a witness pass. Failed candidates can be skipped at that fixed accuracy. No exact threshold equality needs resolution.

**Norm-enclosure distinction.** Root's q supports this operator-norm acceptance rule. It does not by itself promise a Frobenius witness below the same threshold: an additional sqrt(2d) may occur. The protected proof deliberately uses the larger Q=ceil(32D/delta), D=2d, so its Frobenius witness has the needed margin. Root permits a genuine matrix-norm enclosure, which is computable and does not require running a science program. For example, after certified approximation of V=exp(2kX)-I, upper estimates from Tr[(V*V)^p]^(1/(2p)) converge to ||V|| with a dimension-controlled ratio; rational arithmetic and certified scalar roots give any prescribed upper error. One must not substitute the simpler Frobenius norm for the root test without changing its ceiling or tolerance. This is an implementation-contract clarification, not a defect in the stated root proof.

Replacing exp(-t_i X_a) by exp((2k_a-t_i)X_a) has positive duration at least one and costs at most eta_R/L per occurrence. Root's signed coefficients ensure t_i<=1 and t_i>=delta/m. Summing at most L errors gives eta_R, with T_pre<=2Lq^(2d). The recurrence includes both blocks, so it pays actual background aging as well as the plant inverse. Recurring only the plant block would not establish the moving target.

Root then explicitly changes every duration to a positive rational u'_j. Its condition

    |u'_j-u_j|<=min(u_j/2,eta_R/(2ML))

is effectively satisfiable. A uniform stricter rational approximation tolerance min(delta/(4m),eta_R/(4ML)) is available from the known positive lower bound u_j>=delta/m. It avoids deciding whether a computable duration equals a threshold. Unitary Duhamel costs at most eta_R/2, safely rounded up to eta_R in the source. Also u'_j>=delta/(2m) and T<=3Lq^(2d), hence the source's looser 4Lq^(2d) upper recipe.

After this rounding the second block is exactly exp(-i T Hbar) for the **new actual rational T**. Comparing to the old T_pre would be wrong, but root does not do that. All physical scalar phases and pulse areas are recomputed at the new durations.

The protected proof instead retains computable algebraic durations. Every signed commutator has exact duration balance, so replacing its inverse leaves gives T=2t0 sum_negative k_a. It neither asserts that every individual pulse duration is rational nor needs such a promise. Its polynomial minimum-duration and ramp bounds are explicit. A rational schedule can be added with a separate rounding budget by the root method, but doing so changes that protected recipe and exact balance statement; it is not already an uncharged feature of its immutable proof.

## 6. Smoothing, scalar phase and full endpoint comparison

Root's actual rational segment lower bound gives

    rho_min=min(delta/(8m),eta_R/(gL)).

Choosing rho_j=min(u'_j/4,eta_R/(gL)) preserves every segment duration and permits two cubic ramps plus a plateau. Each two-ramp envelope loses area exactly rho_j. The traceless error is g sum_active rho_j<=eta_R. Its physical positive control has norm 2gf, so its actual scalar area must be retained separately as A_s=g sum_active(u'_j-rho_j), which the root source does.

The pre-smoothing augmented error is at most 5eta_R. The plant and aging blocks each satisfy that bound. Therefore the moving-target error is at most 10eta_R before smoothing and 11eta_R afterwards. With eta_R=epsilon_R/16 this is strictly below epsilon_R. The complete channel bound min(2,2epsilon_R) stated by root is conservative and valid. It should not be read as an unhalved trace bound epsilon_R.

For a computable rho_j the peak control derivative is at most 3g/rho_min. If a positive rational ramp width between half the chosen value and the value is used instead, the derivative allowance doubles to 6g/rho_min and the error does not increase. Root states this alternative correctly. All joins have zero value and derivative, so concatenation is C1. Exact computable pulse parameters remain an ideal control contract; physical approximation belongs in the full generator-error budget.

The protected total is separately 15eta_I/32 in operator norm, after its target-grid, signed-word, positive-replacement and smoothing allocations. Its endpoint complete trace tolerance can be eta_I if its additional integrated generator error is at most eta_I/32. These constants use a different construction parameter and cannot be numerically identified with eta_R. Both restore (1) with the actual pulse scalar area, old H scalar and all constant reserves.

Whole-generator positivity follows from H+r0I>=0 and positive J,C, or robustly from r0>=h+zeta_peak with a supplied full-space peak fault bound. It does not prove that all old local channels are separately positive. A consumer demanding the latter needs its declared local decomposition and allocated scalar reserves, with phase/action and fault margins repriced. No augmented coordinate or positive-time proof manufactures that stronger hardware contract.

## 7. Mandatory chronology qualifications and reusable composition

The root readout correctly identifies two statements that must be explicit in any current wrapper.

**Finite products must compose augmented pairs.** Suppose successive target factors are W_j=exp(i theta_j)exp(Q_j), with the same physical background and corresponding port/path setup. Before restoring the central scalars, stage j gives a smoothed pair whose plant error from exp(Q_j) is at most 6eta_j and whose aging error from identity is at most 5eta_j. Multiplication in chronological order gives plant error at most 6sum eta_j from exp(Q_k)...exp(Q_1), and aging error at most 5sum eta_j from identity. The actual second product is exp[-i(sum T_j)Hbar]. Therefore the final actual-aging error is at most 11sum eta_j. The phase is

    chi_total=(r0+lambda j0)sum T_j+sum A_s,j+sum theta_j.

The target is W_total exp[-i(sum T_j)H], with W_total=W_k...W_1. Durations and actions sum; peak fields and slew use their actual maxima; variations and integrated error budgets sum. Endpoint-zero C1 pulses concatenate without a free pause. Changes of H, J or other baseline parameters between stages require their own stated chronological and cost contract and are not covered by this common-baseline formula.

Naively multiplying only W_j exp(-iT_j Hbar) creates interleaved background factors. For example, with Hbar=Z and W_1=-iX, the difference between exp(-itZ)(-iX) and (-iX)exp(-itZ) has operator norm 2|sin t|. This finite analytic witness explains the ordering issue; it is not a counterexample to the root's augmented construction, whose recurrence bounds control the relevant second coordinate. The corrected reusable statement composes the pairs first and reconstructs total aging afterwards.

**The finite window follows H after the target.** The correct window formula is exactly (1). It is generally not W exp[-i(T+s)H]. The same X/Z example witnesses the difference. For each actual s the extra scalar phase is (r0+lambda j0)s and the coherent error adds at most lambda||Jbar||s, bounded by lambda b w uniformly. Using w in place of s inside every comparator would be another chronology/phase mistake. The inherited compiler equation already has the correct formula; the root proposal's abbreviated reference is governed by this explicit qualification.

These two qualifications preserve the source bytes and constants. They do not turn an endpoint compiler into an arbitrary prescribed-time theorem, a permanent stop, a full intermediate target trajectory or an autonomous state supplier.

## 8. Resource, calibration, work and moment limits

For root's actual fixed certificate, delta is bounded above and below by fixed positive multiples of epsilon_R. The displayed sufficient choices give

    m=O(epsilon_R^(-ell)),
    L=O(epsilon_R^(-ell)),
    q=O(epsilon_R^(-(ell+1))),
    T=O(epsilon_R^[-ell-2d(ell+1)]),
    rho_min^(-1)=O(epsilon_R^(-(ell+1))).                  (3)

The empty schedule is handled separately. These upper statements apply to the printed sufficient recipes, not every larger repetition or recurrence choice. The protected exponents match (3) with its own fixed constants and construction tolerance. Root's E_i contains exponential majorants; protected E_i uses unitary Taylor jets but doubles signed basis terms and employs a target grid. Matching exponents is neither equality of constants nor a practical efficiency result.

The complete full norm allowance h+lambda||J||+r0+2g, static scalar rate, all waits, pulse area and T+w action must remain. Positive-block norm sums, Pauli coefficient sums, whole operator norm, scalar action and nominal work are not interchangeable. The one-port control variation is exactly 4g times the number of active segments, hence root's 4gL bound is valid. A constant background has no explicit parameter derivative during this experiment, but its energy changes and its installation are not free thermodynamic claims.

The original review also supplies the useful endpoint work bound, for j=2(L_P-1),

    |W_nom|<=min(4gL_active,2h+lambda j),
    |W_actual-W_nominal|
      <=(h+lambda j/2)min(2,2E_int)
        +||D(T)||+||D(0)||.

The latter assumes the regular full actual work identity and the same initial state. Endpoint-defect bounds suffice; variation/derivative estimates are an alternative. Integrated unitary error alone gives neither endpoint work nor peak positivity. Root does not claim otherwise; this inherited qualification should remain alongside its shorter resource summary. Constant identity reserves disappear from the nominal endpoint energy difference but persist in coherent phase and action.

Every actual generator error is charged over full T+w. If a fixed per-time error floor remains while T grows, no arbitrary-accuracy conclusion follows. Timing faults likewise require the complete nominal dynamics and phase at the actual time, or an explicit full-generator duration error. A common waveform shift can be priced by its total variation; changing observation time is a different comparison. Neither exact recurrence nor exact matrix knowledge is silently robust to hardware defects.

For a retained observable norm B_obs and complete state error e, mean, second moment and variance errors are bounded by B_obs e, B_obs^2 e and 3B_obs^2 e. Growing physical norms in an optional autonomous controller must be charged again. Neither source gives a free thermal state, clock state, bath limit, native waveform actuator, local calibration apparatus, physical energy identification, permanent detector or restored memory bank.

If lambda is fixed and w>0, the allowance lambda b w remains. Shrinking lambda to shrink it changes the basis and may worsen sigma or kappa and the degree/list. Neither proof supplies a uniform lower conditioning bound for that family. Even with fixed lambda, d, certificate length, target-data access and supplied norm bounds cannot vary secretly while (3) is called uniform. A complete autonomous composition must recompute horizon, waveform Lipschitz constant, clock size, mediator penalty and all their physical ledgers. No efficient pipeline theorem is inherited merely by concatenating existence statements.

