## 10. Exposure, source recovery and actual execution

The root proposal, its complete SOURCE_PINS and two-member proposal freeze, the full chronology readout, the protected proof/freeze, and the actual pre-exposure root READ record were read in this comparison. The root metadata program, its actual recorder and stdout were also read. Its captured EXECUTION.json records actual 20:47:00.932135-20:47:01.019098 UTC, exit 0, source at launch, argv and streams; the directory label 2050 is not that timestamp. No missing LAUNCH record is invented.

Both complete old compiler proof and original separate review remain the only mathematical imports. Their prior complete readings are reused at exact pinned bytes. The protected proof's 27 frozen members and eight selected source/recovery identities are checked by the new metadata helpers; root's candidate's two frozen source members are checked separately. Historical publication pins inside SOURCE_PINS are provenance, not extra theorem dependencies or a claim to recover entire publication archives.

The current SOURCE_MANIFEST records every selected identity and its content-addressed recovery. Only necessary proof, qualification, exposure, instruction and actual receipt sources are copied, without recursive old publication bundles. Current capture and verification have their own source-at-launch, argv, stdout/stderr, timeout and exit receipts. These checks establish source integrity only. No numerical predicate or compiler search was used as an independent mathematical check.

No adverse scientific fixture was suppressed or rerun; none was run here. The preserved failures include negative-time substitutions, first-block-only control, arbitrary selected-lambda cancellation, interleaved aging, unpriced windows, uncontrolled calibration/work, oversized-resource upper-bound claims and free reset assumptions. They are scoped counterexamples, not a broad no-go. No model/effort override, agent, other-chat message, W/Git/PR/audit/checkpoint/lock/axiom/prompt edit occurred. Root retains source acceptance and all publication decisions; the fixed campaign deadline remains unchanged.
